{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"custom-client","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Custom client"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Vue Query allows providing custom "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"QueryClient"},{"type":"text","value":" for Vue context."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"It might be handy when you need to create "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"QueryClient"},{"type":"text","value":" beforehand to integrate it with other libraries that do not have access to the Vue context."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For this reason, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"VueQueryPlugin"},{"type":"text","value":" accepts either "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"QueryClientConfig"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"QueryClient"},{"type":"text","value":" as a plugin options."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If You provide "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"QueryClientConfig"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"QueryClient"},{"type":"text","value":" instance will be created internally and provided to Vue context."}]},{"type":"code","value":"const vueQueryPluginOptions: VueQueryPluginOptions = {\n  queryClientConfig: {\n    defaultOptions: { queries: { staleTime: 3600 } },\n  },\n}\napp.use(VueQueryPlugin, vueQueryPluginOptions)","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"code","value":"const myClient = new QueryClient(queryClientConfig)\nconst vueQueryPluginOptions: VueQueryPluginOptions = {\n  queryClient: myClient,\n}\napp.use(VueQueryPlugin, vueQueryPluginOptions)","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"custom-context-key","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Custom context key"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You can also customize the key under which "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"QueryClient"},{"type":"text","value":" will be accessible in Vue context. This can be usefull is you want to avoid name clashing between multiple apps on the same page with Vue2."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"It works both with default, and custom "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"QueryClient"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const vueQueryPluginOptions: VueQueryPluginOptions = {\n  queryClientKey: 'Foo',\n}\napp.use(VueQueryPlugin, vueQueryPluginOptions)","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"code","value":"const myClient = new QueryClient(queryClientConfig)\nconst vueQueryPluginOptions: VueQueryPluginOptions = {\n  queryClient: myClient,\n  queryClientKey: 'Foo',\n}\napp.use(VueQueryPlugin, vueQueryPluginOptions)","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"To use the custom client key, You have to provide it as a query options"}]},{"type":"code","value":"useQuery({\n  queryKey: ['query1'],\n  queryFn: fetcher,\n  queryClientKey: 'foo',\n})","lang":"js"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Internally custom key will be combined with default query key as a suffix. But user do not have to worry about it."}]},{"type":"code","value":"const vueQueryPluginOptions: VueQueryPluginOptions = {\n  queryClientKey: 'Foo',\n}\napp.use(VueQueryPlugin, vueQueryPluginOptions) // -> VUE_QUERY_CLIENT:Foo","lang":"tsx"}],"headings":[{"id":"custom-client","text":"Custom client","level":3},{"id":"custom-context-key","text":"Custom context key","level":3}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n### Custom client\n\nVue Query allows providing custom `QueryClient` for Vue context.\n\nIt might be handy when you need to create `QueryClient` beforehand to integrate it with other libraries that do not have access to the Vue context.\n\nFor this reason, `VueQueryPlugin` accepts either `QueryClientConfig` or `QueryClient` as a plugin options.\n\nIf You provide `QueryClientConfig`, `QueryClient` instance will be created internally and provided to Vue context.\n\n```tsx\nconst vueQueryPluginOptions: VueQueryPluginOptions = {\n  queryClientConfig: {\n    defaultOptions: { queries: { staleTime: 3600 } },\n  },\n}\napp.use(VueQueryPlugin, vueQueryPluginOptions)\n```\n\n```tsx\nconst myClient = new QueryClient(queryClientConfig)\nconst vueQueryPluginOptions: VueQueryPluginOptions = {\n  queryClient: myClient,\n}\napp.use(VueQueryPlugin, vueQueryPluginOptions)\n```\n\n### Custom context key\n\nYou can also customize the key under which `QueryClient` will be accessible in Vue context. This can be usefull is you want to avoid name clashing between multiple apps on the same page with Vue2.\n\nIt works both with default, and custom `QueryClient`\n\n```tsx\nconst vueQueryPluginOptions: VueQueryPluginOptions = {\n  queryClientKey: 'Foo',\n}\napp.use(VueQueryPlugin, vueQueryPluginOptions)\n```\n\n```tsx\nconst myClient = new QueryClient(queryClientConfig)\nconst vueQueryPluginOptions: VueQueryPluginOptions = {\n  queryClient: myClient,\n  queryClientKey: 'Foo',\n}\napp.use(VueQueryPlugin, vueQueryPluginOptions)\n```\n\nTo use the custom client key, You have to provide it as a query options\n\n```js\nuseQuery({\n  queryKey: ['query1'],\n  queryFn: fetcher,\n  queryClientKey: 'foo',\n})\n```\n\nInternally custom key will be combined with default query key as a suffix. But user do not have to worry about it.\n\n```tsx\nconst vueQueryPluginOptions: VueQueryPluginOptions = {\n  queryClientKey: 'Foo',\n}\napp.use(VueQueryPlugin, vueQueryPluginOptions) // -> VUE_QUERY_CLIENT:Foo\n```\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: custom-client\ntitle: Custom Client\n---\n\n### Custom client\n\nVue Query allows providing custom `QueryClient` for Vue context.\n\nIt might be handy when you need to create `QueryClient` beforehand to integrate it with other libraries that do not have access to the Vue context.\n\nFor this reason, `VueQueryPlugin` accepts either `QueryClientConfig` or `QueryClient` as a plugin options.\n\nIf You provide `QueryClientConfig`, `QueryClient` instance will be created internally and provided to Vue context.\n\n```tsx\nconst vueQueryPluginOptions: VueQueryPluginOptions = {\n  queryClientConfig: {\n    defaultOptions: { queries: { staleTime: 3600 } },\n  },\n}\napp.use(VueQueryPlugin, vueQueryPluginOptions)\n```\n\n```tsx\nconst myClient = new QueryClient(queryClientConfig)\nconst vueQueryPluginOptions: VueQueryPluginOptions = {\n  queryClient: myClient,\n}\napp.use(VueQueryPlugin, vueQueryPluginOptions)\n```\n\n### Custom context key\n\nYou can also customize the key under which `QueryClient` will be accessible in Vue context. This can be usefull is you want to avoid name clashing between multiple apps on the same page with Vue2.\n\nIt works both with default, and custom `QueryClient`\n\n```tsx\nconst vueQueryPluginOptions: VueQueryPluginOptions = {\n  queryClientKey: 'Foo',\n}\napp.use(VueQueryPlugin, vueQueryPluginOptions)\n```\n\n```tsx\nconst myClient = new QueryClient(queryClientConfig)\nconst vueQueryPluginOptions: VueQueryPluginOptions = {\n  queryClient: myClient,\n  queryClientKey: 'Foo',\n}\napp.use(VueQueryPlugin, vueQueryPluginOptions)\n```\n\nTo use the custom client key, You have to provide it as a query options\n\n```js\nuseQuery({\n  queryKey: ['query1'],\n  queryFn: fetcher,\n  queryClientKey: 'foo',\n})\n```\n\nInternally custom key will be combined with default query key as a suffix. But user do not have to worry about it.\n\n```tsx\nconst vueQueryPluginOptions: VueQueryPluginOptions = {\n  queryClientKey: 'Foo',\n}\napp.use(VueQueryPlugin, vueQueryPluginOptions) // -> VUE_QUERY_CLIENT:Foo\n```\n"}
